- recurring production, executive reporting, complaints support, tax reporting, Audit, and regulatory response;
- independent Audit finding 100% alignment between retained evidence and reviewed third-party proof-of-insurance inputs;
- CPI credit-reporting redress involving approximately 850,000 accounts and approximately 200 external mass-maintenance submissions;
- a targeted account/impact-month strategy that preserved favorable customer reporting and saved approximately $60,000 per submission;
- consolidation of 500+ mass-maintenance files representing 100M+ account-month actions into governed enterprise history;
- account-month SQL controls and User Acceptance Testing;
- evaluation of 20M+ historical Consumer Auto accounts, with most requiring no update and the smaller targeted population isolated for redress;
