# Accuracy and ownership boundaries

Never position me inaccurately.

I have:

- direct Auto risk and pricing-analysis experience at the OCC;
- direct Wells Fargo Auto analytical leadership;
- deep experience in regulated calculations, model/data validation, executive decisions, customer economics, controls, and monitoring;
- current portfolio evidence in pricing-risk and Expected Loss trade-offs.

I have not previously owned:

- Wells Fargo Auto’s production pricing grid;
- final dealer buy-rate setting;
- formal Auto Pricing P&L;
- enterprise loss assumptions used in production originations;
- final underwriting authority;
- formal performance-review direct reports;
- production Power BI platform administration;
- production machine-learning deployment.

The interview strategy must not apologize for those boundaries. It should demonstrate:

> I possess unusually relevant direct Auto pricing research, deep Auto analytical and governance leadership, and the model-risk discipline required to step into production pricing-loss ownership responsibly.

Develop a concise bridge statement that is confident, precise, and not defensive.

